[E0101] Error: `do` is followed by one statement, not a block
   ╭─[ err/663_a_loop_after_do_refused/main.wip:7:21 ]
   │
 7 │     for n in [1] do { assert(n > 0) }
   │                     ┬
   │                     ╰── a block
   │
   │ Help: drop `do`, for the braced form
   │
   │ Note: a loop's body is one statement after `do`, or statements in braces with no `do`
───╯
[E0101] Error: a loop's body after `do` is one statement, and this is a binding, which would bind for nothing after it
